[$in title:["Errors, options and assertions"]]
[$in description:["Recoverable errors, optional values, local recovery and assertions in Moth."]]
[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
[section, $md:
    # Errors, options and assertions

    Moth separates ordinary absence, recoverable failure and broken invariants.
    Use options for absence, implicit built-in failure for checked numeric work,
    typed `Error!` returns for explicit failure and `assert` only when
    continuing would violate an invariant.

    `catch` protects a selected expression and accepts eligible safety catches
    even when authored arithmetic, a cast or multiple calls cannot fail.
    Eligibility does not create a failure effect. Assertions, resource exhaustion
    and fatal foreign-value integrity guards stay outside `catch`. A foreign
    integrity failure returned through a declared builtin `Error!` slot remains
    a typed `Error` and can be caught under ordinary compatibility rules. The
    Progress matrix owns current support: @../progress (Progress).
]

